    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I get that, but isn't it a bit reductive to say retributive justice is just about \"perpetuating cycles\"? A lot of people argue that certain crimes are so heinous that the only moral response is a proportional punishment to uphold the rule of law and provide justice for the victim. Isn't there a valid moral argument that retributive justice is actually more \"just\" in those cases?",
